   "data": {
    "text": "EDITING & STRUCTURE\nPatch any CV (0 to 10 V) into a jack. 0 V is the item's From setting, 10 V its To.\n\nCV-CC 1: MIDI channel 9, CC 1 to 16\n   1 Featured mains\n   2 Groups in the hour\n   3 Exit\n   4 How often a main is in the season\n   5 Scene change rate\n   6 Sequence lengths\n   7 How a scene begins\n   8 Transition\n   9 Call and response\n  10 Repetition scheme\n  11 Signature image\n  12 Contrast map\n  13 Tension\n  14 Energy\n  15 Visual density\n  16 Constant\nCV-CC 2: MIDI channel 9, CC 17 to 32\n   1 Psych-out shift\n   2 Cut articulation\n   3 Operator feel\n   4 Motif shape\n   5 Cross-cutting\n   6 Reveal timing\n   7 Story point of view\n   8 Scene length\n   9 How the scene ends\n  10 The opening grab\n  11 Ends where it starts\n  12 Multicam angle switching\n  13 Nested scene\n  14 Time and speed\n  15 Shots in order\n  16 suite: Two-person hour\nCV-CC 3: MIDI channel 9, CC 33 to 48\n   1 suite: Build\n   2 suite: Drop\n   3 suite: Signature return\n   4 suite: Crime, Tarantino style\n   5 suite: Horror\n   6 suite: Action\n   7 suite: Western\n   8 suite: Musical\n   9 suite: Documentary\n  10 suite: Surrealist\n  11 suite: Romantic comedy\n  12 suite: Viral short\n  13 suite: Episode cliffhanger\n  14 suite: Stop-motion feel\n  15 suite: The big moment\n  16 pair: When tension peaks, a long silence\nCV-CC 4: MIDI channel 9, CC 49 to 54\n   1 pair: When energy drops, the hold is long\n   2 pair: When suite Build, suite Drop\n   3 pair: When suite Aggressive camera, suite Quiet confession\n   4 pair: When suite Storm, suite Breathing room\n   5 pair: When time slows, the bits in the air hang\n   6 pairs: Long-form shape"
